# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Since #234/#249 removed the `.:/app` bind mount, the image IS the deployed
# artifact: everything `COPY . .` picks up ships to the box and stays in the
# layer history. The build context is the live deploy tree at /opt/rsg-hermes,
# which accumulates ad-hoc `.env` backups and scratch dirs — and the old bare
# `.env` rule matched only that exact path, so five credential-bearing
# `.env.bak*` files would have been baked into the image.

.DS_Store
.git
.venv
.venv-*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
schema_map.json

# Environment files and their ad-hoc backups — secrets, never in the image.
# The runtime gets its config from compose `env_file:`, not from the context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/*.env.*
# ...but the committed placeholder templates hold no secrets and can stay.
!**/*.example

# Backups and scratch that collect in the deploy tree.
**/*.bak
**/*.bak.*
**/*.bak-*
_codex_backups/
.pytest_cache/

# Job-idempotency state lives in the named hermes-state volume mounted at
# /var/lib/hermes (see docker-compose.yml). Never bake a stale copy in at
# /app/.hermes — a stale watermark re-sends an externally visible report.
.hermes/
